  "response": "### Branch\n`retrospective-sentence-length-limit`\n\n### Commit Message\n```text\nstyle: enforce 38-word limit on sentences in validator and style guidelines\n\n- Implements a sentence word-count check in tools/validate.mjs (lintProse)\n- Documents the 38-word limit under the Voice section in input/editorial.md\n- Prevents long compound/multi-clause sentences from lowering Prose scores\n```\n\n### Pull Request\n**Title:** `Retrospective: Limit Sentence Length to 38 Words to Prevent Prose Score Penalties`\n\n**Body:**\n```markdown\n### Evidence from Score History\nAcross prior editions, the paper repeatedly lost points under the **Prose** dimension, scoring a **4** instead of a perfect **5** (including `2026-09-01`, `2026-08-26`, `2026-08-22`, `2026-08-21`, `2026-08-20`, `2026-08-19`, and `2026-08-18`).\n\nThe rubric defines a Prose score of 4 as having *\"one or two sentences [that] are longer than they need to be.\"* The evaluation evidence directly highlights this exact pattern:\n- **2026-09-01**: A single long compound sentence in the CHIVE story's second body paragraph.\n- **2026-08-26**: Two long compound sentences in the Nvidia body paragraph.\n- **2026-08-22**: Two whyItMatters paragraphs that ran too long.\n- **2026-08-20**: Two long compound sentences in the Unitree/Samsung whyItMatters.\n- **2026-08-19**: Long, multi-clause sentences in microsoft-ai-chip-gap and chatgpt-for-teens.\n\n### Specific Fix\n1. **Machine Check**: Added a sentence length linter to `tools/validate.mjs` within the `lintProse` function. It splits paragraphs on sentence punctuation boundaries and issues a warning if any sentence exceeds **38 words**.\n2. **Rule Document**: Updated the house voice guidelines in `input/editorial.md` to explicitly mandate that sentences must be kept under 38 words or split.\n\n### What It Would Have Caught\nThis check would have flagged:\n- The 48-word sentence in the CHIVE story's first body paragraph in the `2026-09-01` edition.\n- The 42-word sentence in the `openai-agents-hack-hugging-face` story in the `2026-09-01` edition.\n- The long compound sentences in the `2026-08-26` Nvidia story body paragraph.\n- The long compound whyItMatters sentences in the `2026-08-20` edition.\n```",
